12. My final recommendation: replace the original plan with AegisMark 2.0
I would not simply add a few corrections to the existing document. I would rewrite the specification around a simpler, more realistic architecture.

Here is the priority order I would enforce:
AegisMark 2.0
Proposed product definition

A privacy-first, local-first, cross-browser bookmark manager with optional end-to-end encrypted synchronization.

Simplicity
Highest priority

A fast, uncluttered bookmarking experience. No unnecessary features or complicated workflows.
Security
Highest priority

Proper key management, encryption, device security, secure synchronization and independently reviewed implementation.
Privacy
Highest priority

Local-first processing, minimal data collection and no plaintext bookmark content on the sync server.
Compatibility
Highest priority

Shared core, browser-specific adapters and separately validated platform builds.
Ownership
Highest priority

Complete source code, IP assignment, independent infrastructure and reproducible builds.

Business model

Free local vault + paid encrypted cloud synchronization.

